# vbrecomp.pin — pins which vbrecomp framework commit this game builds against.
#
# PIN MECHANISM
# -------------
# The authoritative pin is the SUBMODULE GITLINK recorded for `vbrecomp/`
# (see .gitmodules). The committed gitlink SHA *is* the version this game
# builds and ships against; a fresh `git submodule update --init` checks out
# exactly that commit. This file is the human-readable mirror of that gitlink
# (kept in sync) plus the local-dev story below.
#
# LOCAL DEV (Windows): the working-tree `vbrecomp/` is a directory JUNCTION to
# a single shared clone so edits to the framework are live across every game
# repo at once, with no per-repo copy to keep in sync:
#
#     # from this repo's root, once:
#     cmd /c rmdir vbrecomp                 # if a real submodule checkout exists
#     New-Item -ItemType Junction -Path vbrecomp `
#         -Target F:\Projects\virtualboyrecomp\vbrecomp
#
# The junction resolves to a real git repo, so the submodule gitlink still
# reads correctly; CI / fresh clones without the junction get a normal
# submodule checkout at the pinned SHA instead.
#
# ROLL THE PIN FORWARD
# --------------------
#   1. Commit (and push) the new framework commit in vbrecomp.
#   2. In this repo, re-point the gitlink to it and update `sha` below:
#        git -C vbrecomp rev-parse HEAD                 # the new SHA
#        git update-index --add --cacheinfo 160000,<sha>,vbrecomp
#        # (or `git add vbrecomp` when vbrecomp/ is a real submodule checkout)
#   3. Commit this file + the gitlink together.
#
# The gitlink SHA must exist on the submodule's remote, or `submodule update`
# fails for everyone else — push vbrecomp before pinning to its commit.

branch = feat/shadow-enhancements
sha    = beb104caa5a7b0b44c589af6d601b862a1d24504
